==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|eptir}}, {{m|non|eptr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*aftiri||more aft, further behind}}, {{m|gem-pro|*after}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*h₂epóteros||further behind, further away}}, comparative form of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂epó||off, behind}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈɛftɪr/}}
* {{IPA|is|/ˈɛhtɪr/|a=colloquial}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɛftɪr|s=2}}

===Preposition===
{{head|is|preposition}}

# [[after]] (temporal; e.g., ''after Sunday'')
